# Fingerprints for the vendored libutf extracts.
#
# `tests/test_vendor_manifest.py` checks these on every run. "VENDORED, DO NOT
# EDIT" is a comment, and a comment stops nobody: a hand-edit to fix something
# locally, or a re-extraction that ran against a dirty tree, both look exactly
# like the file that was reviewed. This is what makes them look different.
#
# It does not check the copy against libutf — that needs libutf present, and
# these files exist so a build does not. It checks that the bytes are the ones
# somebody verified, which is the part that erodes silently.
#
# Refreshing is meant to be deliberate: re-extract, run the oracle sweep in
# docs/vendoring.md against the real library, then update this file in the
# same commit as the extract.
#
